  "summary": "Purchasing migration adds optional SupplierId on existing StockMovements and a Restrict FK, creates Suppliers, Purchases (unique IdempotencyKey, supplier FK), SupplierLedgerEntries (unique IdempotencyKey and supplier FK), PurchaseLines (purchase cascade and inventory Restrict), and PurchasePayments (purchase cascade and unique idempotency). The supplier, purchase, ledger, and payment record monetary/reference facts remain app-enforced; no numeric CHECK constraints. SupplierLedgerEntries.PurchaseId and PurchasePayments.SupplierId/TreasuryMovementId are not FK-linked, consistent with historical snapshot/idempotency design but merits current model/handler context; no defect inferred from schema alone. Down removes StockMovements.SupplierId FK/column and drops dependent tables; no execution.",
